From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:36:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: Flash A runtime fixes -- privapp allowlist,
 com.lge.os.Build stub, getSlotId redirect, permissive radio (bringup)

The com.lge.os.Build.CA_TARGET stub is what LG's stack uses to choose an IMS
profile: OperatorInfo reads OPERATOR and COUNTRY out of it and everything
downstream follows. Stock burns one value per SKU. This device is a Verizon
V20, so the stub reports VZW.

Deriving those values at runtime from the SIM and serving network was tried
and reverted. It is recorded in IMS.md: replacing the constant with a call
into a helper from the stub's class initializer makes OperatorInfo select
ApnImsGlobal instead of ApnImsVZW, and the global path never initialises on
this device. ImsServiceManager, SIMStateAgent and the ISIM broadcast never
run, the IMS PDN never comes up, and no registration is attempted at all.
